    "text": "An asteroid of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is approaching earth, initially at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math> with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></math> It hite oarth with a speed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math> are radius and mass of earth<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math>, then",
